# `number[]` says nothing of fractions, and most such lists hold integers: a read names no storage and goes by the kind that it finds, and the list is made as an empty list of the engine is
# made with storage for doubles, each integer was asked at every read whether it is an int32 before it was boxed: nine to twelve instructions more at every read than without the type
# f1 = total: a list of numbers. f3 = inner: a list of lists and then a list of numbers. Of the outer list Link says that it stays as made (LinkTables::receiversThatStayAsMade): the read asks it nothing and goes by the kind that it finds
# LoopInvariants is withheld in the runs on f1 and f3: with it a row of tests stands in front of a loop that leaves its list alone, and behind it the read names the storage and the sum is raw (list-reads-in-loops-1)
# RUN(NUMBERS): walk f1 mechanisms=all-Inlining-LoopInvariants
# NUMBERS-LABEL: code f1:Body
# NUMBERS: = GetArrayElement {{*}} level=Expected
# RUN(NEVER): walk f1 mechanisms=all-Inlining-LoopInvariants
# NEVER-NOT: arrayStorage=Double
# RUN(LISTS): walk f3 mechanisms=all-Inlining-LoopInvariants
# LISTS-LABEL: code f3:Body
# LISTS: = GetArrayElement {{*}} level=Proven
# RUN(INNER): walk f3 mechanisms=all-Inlining-LoopInvariants
# INNER-NOT: arrayStorage=Double
# PROGRAM-OF: ../unboxed-numbers/sum-that-goes-round-a-loop-boxed-stays-boxed.ir
